# Shell scripts must be LF everywhere: bash on WSL rejects CRLF
# (`pipefail\r`), and lane worktrees on mixed hosts otherwise churn line
# endings into every merge. (v0.2.5 T-INFRA; bugeventlog 2026-07-16
# tool-check-unrunnable-from-WSL entry.)
#
# Total policy (crlf-extensionless-hardening): catch-all LF with binary and
# Windows-script carve-outs. Extension-keyed shell rules remain as documented
# intent (last match wins for those paths). One pattern per line — git
# attributes do not accept space-separated pattern lists.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.exe binary
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sh text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf
*.bats text eol=lf

# Extensionless shebang scripts (also mirrored under skills/superpowers/.gitattributes)
skills/superpowers/skills/subagent-driven-development/scripts/review-package text eol=lf
skills/superpowers/skills/subagent-driven-development/scripts/sdd-workspace text eol=lf
skills/superpowers/skills/subagent-driven-development/scripts/task-brief text eol=lf
